  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical conducting spheres with negligible volume have <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nC</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nC</mi></math> charges, respectively. They are brought into contact and then separated by a distance of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>. The electrostatic force acting between the spheres is ___<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.<br />[Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#960;</mi><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>9</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math> SI unit]",
